.TH BOSWAS-SESSION 1 "November 2026" "Boswas OS" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
boswas-session \- start the Boswas OS desktop session
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B boswas-session
[\fICOMPOSITOR-OPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B boswas-session
is the program
.BR greetd (1)
starts after a successful login. It
.IP \(bu 2
reads the login profile (\fI/etc/profile\fR, \fI~/.profile\fR),
.IP \(bu 2
sets the session's environment (\fBXDG_CURRENT_DESKTOP=Boswas\fR, Wayland
for Qt, GTK, SDL and Firefox, the Boswas defaults for KDE applications),
.IP \(bu 2
starts
.BR boswas-compositor (1),
which starts the shell,
.IP \(bu 2
publishes the session to the user's systemd manager and D-Bus and starts
\fBboswas\-session.target\fR (and with it \fBgraphical\-session.target\fR:
the device session agent, portals, autostart entries; the shell itself is
the polkit authentication agent),
.IP \(bu 2
stops that target when the compositor exits.
.PP
Options are passed on to the compositor.
.SH WHEN THE DESKTOP CANNOT START
A boot never ends without a way to sign in:
.IP \(bu 2
If the login screen cannot be shown (no usable graphics device, no seat,
a login screen that keeps failing), the greeter script
.I /usr/libexec/boswas/boswas\-greeter
starts greetd's text login instead. Signing in there gives the user's
shell on the console
.RI ( /usr/libexec/boswas/boswas\-text\-session ),
with a note on how to try the desktop
.RB ( boswas\-session )
and where to look for the reason.
.IP \(bu 2
If greetd itself cannot run and systemd stops restarting it, the text
login of the first virtual terminal is started in its place
.RI ( boswas\-login\-fallback.service ).
.IP \(bu 2
The other virtual terminals (Ctrl+Alt+F2 to F6) keep their text logins.
.PP
The messages of the compositor and of the programs it starts go to the
journal, not to the console: those of a session under the identifier
\fBboswas\-session\fR (\fBjournalctl \-b \-t boswas\-session\fR), those of
the login screen under \fBboswas\-greeter\fR (readable by an
administrator). Without the journal they stay on standard error.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/wayland\-sessions/boswas.desktop
The session entry.
.TP
.I /etc/boswas/greetd.toml
The login configuration greetd reads on Boswas OS.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/systemd/user/boswas\-session.target
The session target.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/systemd/system/greetd.service.d/10\-boswas.conf
Points greetd at the Boswas login configuration and brings the text login
back if greetd fails for good.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR boswas-compositor (1),
.BR boswas-shell (1),
.BR greetd (1)
